{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of a pyramid whose base is an equilateral triangle of side length 6 and whose other edges are each of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f6d1e000d3e8c4cb552e4905ed41ad2fa540bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41aa2335e872648b4c4abb69467a683e9f31819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 9/2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 27/2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{9\\sqrt3}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"509\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d9124a410a03d7559abebfc6a428d8cfb2d5f34d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; unitsize(1cm); size(200); draw((0,0,0)--(6,0,0)--(3,5.196,0)--(0,0,0)); draw((3,1.732,1.732)--(0,0,0)); draw((3,1.732,1.732)--(6,0,0)); draw((3,1.732,1.732)--(3,5.196,0)); draw((3,1.732,1.732)--(3,1.732,0)--(0,0,0),dotted); label(&quot;6&quot;,(4.5,2.598,0),SW); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{15}$&quot;,(4.5,0.866,0.866),N);  currentprojection=orthographic(1/6,1/2,1/3);  [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p>Draw an altitude towards the equilateral triangle base.  By symmetry (this can also be proved by HL), the base of the altitude is equidistant from the three points of the equilateral triangle.  This means that the distance from the base of the altitude to one of the points of the equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965a47a13fb897421cd3a9a653267ffc5ed17e55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,1.732)--(0,0)--(3.464,0),dotted); draw((0,1.732)--(3.464,0)); label(&quot;$2\\sqrt{3}$&quot;,(1.732,0),S); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{15}$&quot;,(1.732,0.866),NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"155\" />\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, the length of the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, so the volume of the triangular pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f24fb7d72ea4b691eb94e1d14578fc6c7a8427.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac13 \\cdot \\tfrac{6^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"179\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=